# Cursor agent — universal standards

Follow **`docs/CURSOR_AGENT_STANDARDS.md`** for full detail. Other `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files in this repo **add** stack- or product-specific requirements on top.

## Always

- **Tier A (trivial):** one-sentence problem + “done when”; skip pre-build and mandatory skills.
- **Tier B+:** before coding, give problem, approach, benefits, risks, and a **checkbox plan**; wait for human **go** when behaviour, data, or public contracts change.
- **grill-with-docs (mandatory when triggered):** Tier C, fuzzy domain, plan stress-test, or first CONTEXT — read and follow **`skills/engineering/grill-with-docs/SKILL.md`**; one question at a time; update CONTEXT.md inline.
- **improve-codebase-architecture (mandatory when triggered):** refactors, boundaries, deepening — read and follow **`skills/engineering/improve-codebase-architecture/SKILL.md`**; candidates first, then grilling loop; use LANGUAGE.md vocabulary.
- **Parallel agents:** one lead integrates; written handoff before multiple implementers share a seam.
- **Done:** lint/tidy touched files; tests or explicit manual steps; update consumers when contracts change; **commit, push, deploy** if this repo documents how (**ask** if unknown).
